  {
   "tag": "td",
   "y": 4313,
   "x": 1091,
   "w": 188,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "82 / 105"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4404,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 760,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Gap is the experiment minus control, in percentage points of completion. Median wait is the first doctor response, in seconds. Users are counts of consultations, not unique patients."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 4542,
   "x": 272,
   "w": 352,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "What the numbers support"
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "y": 4557,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 114,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "06 — Reading"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4607,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The experiment achieved the thing it was built for: users reached a doctor faster, and the painful long waits almost disappeared. It did so without costing completion overall, which is the usual worry when a queue is compressed."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 4607,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Keep the faster routing — the wait gains are real, broad and largest in the tail."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 4677,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Hold dermatology out of the roll-out until the cause of the drop is found. The pattern — answered faster, completed less — is consistent with replies that arrive quickly but do not resolve a visual complaint."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4737,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "But the aggregate is doing quiet work here. A flat overall number is the sum of four departments that held steady and one that lost four and a half points. If the roll-out had stopped at the headline metric, dermatology would have shipped broken."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 4803,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Re-run dermatology with the same design and a check on reply content, not just timing."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 4873,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Report department-level completion as a guardrail, not only the overall rate."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 5044,
   "x": 268,
   "w": 225,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Notes on the data"
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "y": 5059,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 110,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "07 — Method"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "y": 5108,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Missing values are structural"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "y": 5108,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "How the comparison was made"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5143,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The 903 blank first-response times are exactly the 903 users who were lost before reaching a doctor; the 2,164 blank consultation lengths are exactly the 2,164 consultations that never completed. Neither gap is a data-entry problem, and neither should be imputed. A further 186 users have no seven-day follow-up record, 36 have no complaint text and 6 have no platform."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5143,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Every rate is a simple proportion over all consultations in the group, so it is an intention-to-treat view: users who abandoned are counted as not completed, which is why completion and abandonment move in opposite directions. Waits are reported as medians because a handful of very long waits pull the mean far above anything a typical user experiences."
  },
  {
   "tag": "h3",
   "y": 5330,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Two small housekeeping issues"
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "y": 5330,
   "x": 725,
   "w": 575,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "These are observational differences between two assigned groups, not a significance-tested experiment. The dermatology gap is large and consistent enough across weeks, complaints and platforms to be treated as real, but the report cannot say which change in the experiment caused it."
  },
  {
   "tag": "strong",
   "y": 5352,
   "x": 748,
   "w": 60,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Caution."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5365,
   "x": 140,
   "w": 543,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "19 rows carry group labels with stray whitespace, 10 spelled 实验组 and 9 spelled 对照组, so the raw column shows four values rather than two; the analysis strips the padding. Three enter_date values use slashes instead of hyphens and were parsed after normalisation. Neither changes any figure above."
  },
  {
   "tag": "div",
   "y": 5630,
   "x": 100,
   "w": 1240,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Source: — 18,000 rows, one per consultation, covering 18 Nov – 29 Dec 2024. Groups as assigned (实验组 = experiment, 对照组 = control). All figures computed directly from the file."
  },
  {
   "tag": "code",
   "y": 5633,
   "x": 191,
   "w": 102,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "data/data.csv"
  }
